title: Loop2_Declarations
tags: setup
---
// Never run this node. It only holds variable declarations for Loop 2.

<<declare $loop2_found_letter = false>>
<<declare $loop2_plan = "">>
<<declare $loop2_ordered_food = false>>
<<declare $loop2_lila_ayam = "">>
<<declare $loop2_searched_desk = false>>
<<declare $loop2_searched_bed = false>>
<<declare $loop2_has_recipe = false>>
===

title: Loop2_Start
tags: cutscene locker
---
<<scene_load "LockerRoom" "Morning">>
// Anin arrives at school and goes straight to the locker room to drop off and pick up a few things.
<<quest_start "loop2_crush" "Check your locker.">>
<<give_control>>
===

title: Loop2_Locker
tags: interactable locker
---
<<if $loop2_found_letter>>
    Anin: (Nothing else in here.)
<<else>>
    <<set $loop2_found_letter to true>>
    // Anin finds a blank love letter. Only the recipient's name is written on it: Fal.
    // NEW LINES (no narrator): these three thoughts replace the narration.
    Anin: (A love letter? It's blank... only "Fal" written on the front.)
    Anin: (I've liked him for so long and never did anything about it.)
    Anin: (But if every day is December 10th, I've got all the time in the world. Might as well try.)
    <<item_get "love_letter">>
    <<quest_update "loop2_crush" "Talk to the girls in the classroom.">>
<<endif>>
===

title: Loop2_LockerRoom_Door
tags: interactable locker
---
<<if $loop2_found_letter>>
    Anin: Head to the classroom?
    -> Yes
        <<scene_load "Classroom" "Morning">>
        <<jump Loop2_Classroom>>
    -> No
        // Closes the dialogue.
<<endif>>
===

title: Loop2_Classroom
tags: cutscene classroom
---
Anin: Girls, I need help.
Kirana: What's the matter?
Anin: Help me with a love problem.
Dira: OHHHHH, Anin finally has the guts to make a move!
Lila: Is it Fal?
Anin: Sadly, yes.
Anin: If only there were another option.
Kirana: So what's your plan?
-> Get some information from his friends first.
    <<set $loop2_plan to "info">>
    Anin: I was thinking of getting some information from his friends first.
    Kirana: I bet 10k rupiah you won't get anything out of them. Those guys just mess around and never take anything seriously. They're literally Lila if she were a guy.
    Dira: It's still a good idea, though. How about we sit next to Fal's group during lunch break and listen to their conversation? Maybe we'll pick something up.
-> Ask him to have lunch together.
    <<set $loop2_plan to "direct">>
    Anin: I was thinking of approaching him directly and asking if he wants to have lunch together.
    Kirana: Hold your horses, cowboy. You can't just approach someone like that. You need some kind of introduction phase first.
    Dira: Kirana's right, we need a plan first. How about we gather some information? We could sit next to Fal's group during lunch and listen to their conversation. Maybe we'll pick something up.
Lila: Alright, plan secured. Sorry, Warmus lady, we can't eat your bakwan today.
<<quest_update "loop2_crush" "Gather information on Fal at lunch.">>
<<scene_load "Cafeteria" "Noon">>
<<jump Loop2_Lunch>>
===

title: Loop2_Lunch
tags: cutscene cafeteria
---
// The girls grab an empty table right next to Fal's group.
Kirana: Alright, here's the plan. I'll go over and ask them some questions that might help us learn more about Fal. Dira, you take notes from this table. Anin, you order our food so they won't suspect anything. And Lila... hmm, I don't know, you can just go home.
Lila: Well, screw you.
Dira: That's a good plan. This way we can gather a lot of information without them noticing. I'd like Nasi Pecel, please. Thank you.
Kirana: I'll get Nasi Goreng.
Lila: And I'll have Ayam G—
Kirana: Alright, that's it. Just go, and leave the rest to us.
// Kirana pushes Anin off before Lila can finish.
<<quest_start "lunch_order" "Order food for everyone.">>
<<minimap_set_marker "Warmus">>
<<give_control>>
===

title: Loop2_Cafeteria_Warmus
tags: interactable cafeteria
---
<<if $loop2_ordered_food>>
    Anin: (I should bring the food back before it gets cold.)
<<else>>
    Anin: One Nasi Pecel, one Nasi Goreng, and...
    Anin: (Wait. What did Lila want again? Ayam G-something...)
    -> Ayam Goreng
        <<set $loop2_lila_ayam to "goreng">>
    -> Ayam Gepuk
        <<set $loop2_lila_ayam to "gepuk">>
    -> Ayam Geprek
        <<set $loop2_lila_ayam to "geprek">>
    <<set $loop2_ordered_food to true>>
    <<quest_complete "lunch_order">>
    // By the time Anin gets back, Fal's group has already left.
    <<jump Loop2_LunchRecap>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Loop2_LunchRecap
tags: cutscene cafeteria
---
Anin: Food's here.
// TODO: optional Lila reaction to $loop2_lila_ayam (right/wrong ayam).
Dira: Thanks, Anin. Let's recap what we have. Fal loves playing basketball, and he goes swimming on weekends. Because he's into sports, he eats a lot. He loves anything with chicken, so that should be easy to work with. So, what's the plan?
Kirana: What if you ask him to have dinner with you?
Dira: Or just buy something from Warmus, give it to him, and call it a day?
Anin: That feels too rushed.
Anin: Maybe I'll just buy Ayam Geprek from Warmus.
Lila: Orrr... what if you cook something for him before dinner?
Anin: Hmm, that sounds fun. But what should we cook?
Kirana: Let's go to our dorm and look for the recipe my mom wrote for me.
<<quest_update "loop2_crush" "Find Kirana's mom's recipe.">>
<<scene_load "Dorm" "Afternoon">>
<<jump Loop2_DormSearch>>
===

title: Loop2_DormSearch
tags: cutscene dorm
---
// Anin and Kirana enter their room.
Kirana: Okay, let's start looking. You take your side of the room and I'll take mine. Look for a white sheet of paper with the recipe on it.
<<search_mode_start "recipe">>
<<give_control>>
===

title: Loop2_Dorm_Desk
tags: interactable dorm
---
<<set $loop2_searched_desk to true>>
Anin: (Nothing here, just a bunch of math notes. Ugh, I hate math.)
<<if $loop2_searched_desk and $loop2_searched_bed>>
    <<jump Loop2_DormSearchResult>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Loop2_Dorm_Bed
tags: interactable dorm
---
<<set $loop2_searched_bed to true>>
Anin: (Nope, just a bunch of boxes lying around.)
<<if $loop2_searched_desk and $loop2_searched_bed>>
    <<jump Loop2_DormSearchResult>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Loop2_DormSearchResult
tags: cutscene dorm
---
<<search_mode_end "recipe">>
Kirana: Found anything? There's nothing on my side.
Anin: Nothing on mine either. No paper with a recipe on it.
Anin: You didn't throw it in the trash, did you?
Kirana: I would never throw away something from my family.
Anin: When was the last time you saw it?
Kirana: I remember bringing it to school because a student from the Photography Club asked me to share it with her. She's been into home cooking content lately. But I forgot where I put it after that.
Anin: If only there were a way to turn back time.
// Anin gets a strange feeling, like she could rewind a video. Except instead of a video, she can leap back into a previous loop.
// NEW LINE (no narrator): replaces the narration above.
Anin: (...Wait. What is this feeling? It's like I could rewind everything. Back to the festival.)
<<unlock_ability "time_leap">>
<<time_leap 1>>
<<scene_load "Dorm" "Festival">>
<<jump Loop2_Leap_Arrival>>
===

title: Loop2_Leap_Arrival
tags: cutscene dorm leap
---
// Happy chatter from students fills the dorm.
<<sfx "dorm_crowd">>
Happy Student: What should we eat at the bazaar? OMG, I want to try everything!
Anin: Wait, where's Kirana? Did I really just leap back to the first loop? Let me check outside.
<<quest_update "loop2_crush" "Find Kirana at the festival.">>
<<give_control>>
===

title: Loop2_Leap_DormDoor
tags: interactable dorm leap
---
Anin: Leave the room?
-> Yes
    // Anin has leapt back to the first loop, the day of the school festival.
    <<minimap_show>>
    <<minimap_set_event_marker "SchoolPark">>
    <<scene_load "SchoolPark" "Festival">>
    <<jump Loop2_Leap_Park>>
-> Later
    // Closes the dialogue.
===

title: Loop2_Leap_Park
tags: cutscene park leap
---
Anin: That's Kirana and the Photography Club student. Is that the recipe we're looking for?
Kirana: Here's my mom's sweet soy chicken recipe. Now, can we do the photoshoot like we agreed?
Photography Club Student: Thank you so much, Kirana! I bet it'll taste amazing and look great on camera. Let's go to the photography room.
Anin: They're heading straight to the photography room. So that's how Kirana got her photoshoot.
<<minimap_set_marker "PhotographyClub">>
<<scene_load "PhotographyClub" "Festival">>
<<jump Loop2_Leap_Club>>
===

title: Loop2_Leap_Club
tags: cutscene club leap
---
// Kirana and the Photography Club student are busy taking photos, so focused that they don't even notice Anin.
Anin: (Would confronting them ruin the timeline?)
Anin: (Nah, I don't want to risk it.)
<<quest_update "loop2_crush" "Take the recipe without being noticed.">>
<<give_control>>
===

title: Loop2_Club_Recipe
tags: interactable club leap
---
<<if not $loop2_has_recipe>>
    <<set $loop2_has_recipe to true>>
    // Anin quietly takes the recipe and leaves.
    <<item_get "kirana_recipe">>
    // She heads back to the dorm. Just before entering the room, she leaps back to Loop 2.
    <<time_leap 2>>
    <<scene_load "Dorm" "Afternoon">>
    <<jump Loop2_RecipeFound>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Loop2_RecipeFound
tags: cutscene dorm
---
Anin: Oh, I found it! It was under my bed.
Kirana: Wait, didn't you already check there?
Anin: Must've missed a spot. Okay, sweet soy chicken... we need sweet soy sauce, chicken breast, and the special seasoning. I think we already have all of that in the fridge.
Kirana: Let's head to the kitchen.
<<quest_update "loop2_crush" "Cook the sweet soy chicken.">>
<<scene_load "Kitchen" "Afternoon">>
<<cooking_start "sweet_soy_chicken">>
// Cooking steps (handled in Unity):
// 1. Take the chicken from the fridge
// 2. Rinse it under running water
// 3. Chop it on the cutting board
// 4. Rub the sweet soy sauce into the chicken
// 5. Sprinkle the special seasoning over it
// 6. Cook it in the pan
// When the minigame finishes, Unity should start node Loop2_CookingDone.
<<give_control>>
===

title: Loop2_CookingDone
tags: cutscene kitchen
---
Anin: Finally. Not perfect, but it looks good.
Lila: Before you give it to Fal, I suggest letting me taste it first. Just to make sure it's good.
Kirana: Nahhh, you just want a bite for yourself. Go get ready to give it to Fal, Anin. Don't mind her.
<<quest_update "loop2_crush" "Give the chicken to Fal.">>
<<scene_load "LockerRoom" "Evening">>
<<jump Loop2_Fal>>
===

title: Loop2_Fal
tags: cutscene locker
---
// Anin waits at the locker room. A few minutes later, Fal appears.
Fal: Oh, hi Anin. What's up? You haven't gone home yet?
Anin: Nope. Ugh, not yet.
Fal: Alright then, see ya.
Anin: Actually, I was looking for you.
Fal: Oh, what is it?
Anin: Here. My friends and I cooked dinner, and it turned out we made too much. Do you want some? It's chicken with sweet soy sauce. We used Kirana's mom's recipe.
Fal: Oh, for me? Sure, uh... thanks, Anin. Mmm, it smells so good.
Fal: Chicken's my favorite, actually. Cheap, filling, protein.
Anin: Uhh, yeah, I already know that.
Fal: Wait, you knew? How?
Anin: N-no! I said I could already tell that.
// (beat)
Anin: You just... look like a chicken guy.
Fal: ...A chicken guy?
Anin: Yeah. You're always so loud in the morning, it wakes everyone up right before class. The morning class teacher should be thanking you.
Fal: Wow. Okay. I'll take that as a compliment, I guess.
Fal: Alright, I'll have this for dinner. Thanks, Anin.
Fal: Oh, by the way, there's an exam coming up. Do you have some free time to help me with math? I heard from a guy on the basketball team that you're good at it.
Anin: I wouldn't say I'm good, but I do know math. But, um... sure, if you want to study together.
Fal: Sweet. I'll see you after lunch break, if that's cool. See ya, Anin.
Anin: See ya!
Anin: (I can't believe I just talked to him so casually.)
Anin: (I think it's time to go to bed.)
<<quest_complete "loop2_crush">>
<<scene_load "Dorm" "Night">>
<<jump Loop2_End>>
===

title: Loop2_End
tags: cutscene dorm
---
Kirana: OMG, ANIN, YOU ACTUALLY DID IT!
Lila: WHAT DID HE SAY??
Dira: You did it, Anin. Now the rest is up to you.
Anin: I couldn't have done it without you. Thanks, girls.
<<loop_end 2>>
===
